  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}x^k & x^{k+2} & x^{k+3} \\\\ y^k & y^{k+2} & y^{k+3} \\\\ z^k & z^{k+2} & z^{k+3}\\end{array}\\right|=(x-y)(y-z)(z-x)\\left(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}\\right)$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DXJXo",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{k}=-3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "x6CHW",
      "text": "k=3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zS8sH",
      "text": "k=1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "48S9X",
      "text": "k=-1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} \\text { Hint : } & (x y z)^k\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & x^2 & x^3 \\\\ 1 & y^2 & y^3 \\\\ 1 & z^2 & z^3\\end{array}\\right| \\\\ & =(x y z)^k(x-y)(z-x)-(y-z)(x y+y z+z x) \\\\ & =(x y z)^{k+1}(x-y)(z-x)-(y-z)\\left(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}\\right) \\\\ & k+1=0 \\\\ & k=-1\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
